{
  "version": 1,
  "name": "Lau 2026: circular patch R/d = 0.1, below J_max (RZ)",
  "description": "Lau, Chernin, Heri & Zhang, arXiv:2607.24590 (2026): circular emitting patch of radius R = 0.1 d in a planar diode (RZ), confined flow (z-only motion), injection energy Delta = 0.01, V0 = 2.5 kV, d = 1 cm; outer surface r = d with dphi/dr = 0. Mesh refined over the patch and in front of the cathode. Steady-state limit (Eq. 7 in r-z, picstudio.core.confined_flow): J_max = 5.872 J_CL. First-order estimate, paper Eqs. (5)/(B10): 1.328 (R/d)^-1/2 [1 + 0.34 (R/d)^1.5] (valid for Delta << R/d, an upper estimate). Below J_max all current reaches the anode; above it a virtual cathode forms (phi_min -> -Delta*V0, I_cathode < 0). Magnetic field: Species > motion = z_only is the infinite axial field (electrons move only along z, the assumption of Luginsland et al. 1996 and Lau 2001); motion = full uses the applied field 'axial B' = [Bz, 0, 0] T with the parameter Bz (0 = no field, or any finite value, e.g. 0.1, 1, 10).",
